<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="trinkets-for-retribution-paladin-dps">Trinkets for Retribution Paladin DPS</h4>For Trinkets, the most optimal setup is to have 1 active on-use trinket and 1 passive proc/<wbr/>trigger trinket. Due to this, we typically compare passive trinkets against each other and active trinkets against each other when ranking them, thus we will separate the trinket rankings into two charts - active trinkets and passive trinkets.<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="active-trinkets">Active Trinkets</h5>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=68712/impatience-of-youth">
<img alt="Impatience of Youth" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_idol_05.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Impatience of Youth</span></a> is both our pre-raid best in slot and Phase 1 best in slot, and the most powerful trinket listed here - start doing your <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/zone=5095/tol-barad">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Tol Barad</span></a> dailies as soon as possible. The next-best option is the Jewelcrafting trinket <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=52351/figurine-king-of-boars">
<img alt="Figurine - King of Boars" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_goldenboar.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Figurine - King of Boars</span></a>, which has a 20-second duration and a 2-minute cooldown that lines up perfectly with cooldowns. The rest of the active trinkets have a 15 second duration and a 90 second cooldown, causing them spend less time overlapped with your cooldowns and hurting their value; <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=56285/might-of-the-ocean">
<img alt="Might of the Ocean" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_stone_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Might of the Ocean</span></a> and <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=56345/magnetite-mirror">
<img alt="Magnetite Mirror" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_stone_sharpeningstone_05.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Magnetite Mirror</span></a> are the same trinket just with the passive stat being hit or expertise, and since hit is more valuable and harder to overcap, <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=56285/might-of-the-ocean">
<img alt="Might of the Ocean" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_stone_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Might of the Ocean</span></a> is the better option. <br/>
<br/>
<i>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=59461/fury-of-angerforge">
<img alt="Fury of Angerforge" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cat_trinket08.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fury of Angerforge</span></a> is not listed here because it is wildly expensive and takes forever to stack due to a 5-second internal cooldown. You should NOT spend money on it. </i>
